{"id": "EUVD-2026-59559", "enisaUuid": "9334c434-ae36-3c75-b04d-7b37ae21ce06", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: rtw88: fix wrong pci_get_drvdata type in AER handlers\n\nrtw88 stores an ieee80211_hw pointer via pci_set_drvdata() at probe\ntime, but io_error_detected() and io_resume() retrieve it as a\nnet_device pointer.  This causes netif_device_detach/attach to\noperate on an ieee80211_hw struct, reading and writing at wrong\noffsets.\n\nUse ieee80211_stop_queues/wake_queues instead, consistent with\nevery other queue stop/start path in the driver.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:59:19", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T19:05:44", "baseScore": 8.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:A/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1ef3d1338d94ec41f58fbfb6ba7742a27ea61d89", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d7920797f721f944861f3c48ffb2b73f84b631fe", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/706183dbef4a79d120d4e928f693bea50df496f8"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74412", "GHSA-r36v-qwfg-3x64"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.38, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07be5cb8-4aee-3bdc-9054-82470dd30d45", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "0bcccc1d-7056-3aa9-9002-0b12bb2890c0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cdb82c80b9349ed1d9ce6b49856128e04f4effc9 <706183dbef4a79d120d4e928f693bea50df496f8"}, {"id": "1ebce3f2-c5bc-3dea-8665-3a76a9f55492", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cdb82c80b9349ed1d9ce6b49856128e04f4effc9 <1ef3d1338d94ec41f58fbfb6ba7742a27ea61d89"}, {"id": "2e1a10bc-9382-3ec4-83e5-392e0d0374e3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.17"}, {"id": "57bdc5cb-2054-3a47-b444-16993ad87e6a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "cdb82c80b934